"""HTML and scoped JavaScript for directly interpretable vocabulary comparisons."""
import json,html,base64
def panel(O):
 r=json.loads((O/'full250/analysis/similarity_breakdown.json').read_text('utf8'));esc=lambda x:html.escape(str(x))
 image='data:image/png;base64,'+base64.b64encode((O/'full250/figures/wording_similarity_matrix.png').read_bytes()).decode()
 axes=''.join('<tr><td>Component '+str(a['component'])+'</td><td>'+f'{a["variance_share"]*100:.1f}%</td><td>'+esc(', '.join(a['positive_words']))+'</td><td>'+esc(', '.join(a['negative_words']) or 'No negative weights')+'</td></tr>' for a in r['old_components'])
 markup=f'''<p>We compare the vocabulary in <b>48 selected English texts</b>: 45 national approval pathways, two narrower texts and one official explanation. Each country is compared with every other country using the full vocabulary, with repeated country and agency names removed.</p>
<figure><img src="{image}" alt="48 by 48 matrix of country text similarity, ordered by hierarchical clustering"><figcaption>Both axes list the same countries. Darker squares mean more similar vocabulary; the diagonal is each text compared with itself. Hierarchical clustering places countries with similar word use next to one another. It orders the countries without imposing a fixed number of legal groups. Country codes and full names appear in the selector below.</figcaption></figure>
<h3>Break down one country’s closest matches</h3><label for="similarityCountry">Choose a country in the English-text sample</label><select id="similarityCountry"></select><div id="similarityMatches"></div>
<p class="small">The score is cosine similarity × 100: 100 means the same weighted vocabulary profile, and 0 means no vocabulary overlap in the retained terms. It is not a probability, a percentage of identical clauses, or a measure of legal equivalence. Shared words below are the largest contributions to each pair’s score; related word endings are combined.</p>
<details class="context-details"><summary>What did components 1 and 2 in the old graph mean?</summary><p>The old graph used latent semantic analysis (a two-component truncated singular-value decomposition). Each component is a weighted combination of words chosen mathematically to summarise the texts. Component 1 mainly captures shared approval vocabulary. Component 2 separates European mutual-recognition language from registration and assessment language. The sign of an axis is arbitrary.</p><p>Together the two axes account for <b>{sum(a['variance_share'] for a in r['old_components'])*100:.1f}% of cross-text variation</b>. Neither axis directly measures regulatory strictness, delay, cost or reliance intensity. The matrix above uses the full vocabulary instead of compressing it into two axes.</p><div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Old axis</th><th>Variation explained</th><th>Words with largest positive weights</th><th>Words with largest negative weights</th></tr></thead><tbody>{axes}</tbody></table></div></details>
<p>The median selected national text expressly mentions <b>2 of 11 tracked requirement dimensions</b> (middle half: 1–4). This counts documented conditions. Source length, document type and shared legal systems affect both wording similarity and the number of conditions observed.</p>'''
 js="const SIM="+json.dumps(r,ensure_ascii=False).replace('</','<\\/')+r''';
document.getElementById('similarityCountry').innerHTML=SIM.countries.slice().sort((a,b)=>a.country.localeCompare(b.country)).map(c=>'<option value="'+esc(c.iso3)+'">'+esc(c.country)+' ('+esc(c.iso3)+')</option>').join('');
document.getElementById('similarityCountry').value='GBR';
function renderSimilarity(){const iso=document.getElementById('similarityCountry').value;document.getElementById('similarityMatches').innerHTML='<table><thead><tr><th>Closest country text</th><th>Similarity, 0–100</th><th>Words contributing most to the match</th></tr></thead><tbody>'+SIM.neighbors[iso].slice(0,5).map(c=>'<tr><td>'+esc(c.country)+' ('+esc(c.iso3)+')</td><td><b>'+c.score.toFixed(1)+'</b><div style="height:7px;background:#dce8df;max-width:150px"><div style="height:7px;background:#176b64;width:'+c.score+'%"></div></div></td><td>'+esc(c.shared_words.join(', '))+'</td></tr>').join('')+'</tbody></table>';}
document.getElementById('similarityCountry').addEventListener('change',renderSimilarity);renderSimilarity();
'''
 return markup,js
